# Inky Frame API — scratch requests (JetBrains HTTP client).
# Set host to your Pi.
@host = http://inky-frame.local:8080

### Liveness
GET {{host}}/healthz

### Status (driver, busy, last error, MQTT connection)
GET {{host}}/status

### Send a photo (raw body) and show it. This is what the iOS Shortcut does.
POST {{host}}/display/image
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./data/sample.jpg

### Render only (no panel refresh) — tune dithering, then fetch the preview
POST {{host}}/display/image?show=false&fit=contain
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./data/sample.jpg

### Fetch the last rendered image
GET {{host}}/display/preview

### Block until the refresh finishes (~30s)
POST {{host}}/display/image?wait=true
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./data/sample.jpg

### Blank the panel
POST {{host}}/display/clear

### Guest Wi-Fi dashboard (the only dashboard; pre-composed, shown with dither=NONE)
POST {{host}}/display/dashboard?name=guest_wifi

### --- Photo library (photos, their renders, collections) --------------------

### Upload WITHOUT rendering or showing (what the gallery's + button does)
POST {{host}}/library?name=Sunset
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./data/sample.jpg

### Index. Each entry lists every render made from it.
GET {{host}}/library?limit=20

### One photo
GET {{host}}/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef

### Its files
GET {{host}}/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef/thumb
GET {{host}}/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef/original

### Make (or reuse) a render — the key is a hash of these parameters
POST {{host}}/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef/render?fit=cover&rotate=90&dither=ATKINSON

### ...or place an explicit rectangle, which is what the crop editor sends. x,y,w,h in
### pixels of the ROTATED photo; it may extend past the edges (that becomes white).
POST {{host}}/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef/render?crop=120,0,1600,1200&dither=ATKINSON

### That render, and its thumbnail
GET {{host}}/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef/renders/abc1234567
GET {{host}}/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef/renders/abc1234567/thumb

### Put a saved render back on the panel verbatim — nothing is recomputed
POST {{host}}/display/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef?render=abc1234567

### ...or render it afresh with the current settings
POST {{host}}/display/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef

### Step through the library (reuses each photo's latest render)
POST {{host}}/display/nav?direction=next

### Fetch an image by URL and show it
POST {{host}}/display/url?url=http://homeassistant.local:8123/media/local/photo.jpg

### Drop one render, keep the photo
DELETE {{host}}/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef/renders/abc1234567

### Forget a photo entirely (original, thumb and every render)
DELETE {{host}}/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef

### --- Collections (a photo can be in several) --------------------------------

GET {{host}}/collections

### Create one
POST {{host}}/collections
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Guests"}

### Only the photos in it
GET {{host}}/library?collection=c-1a2b3c4d

### Set which collections a photo is in (the full set, like a row of checkboxes)
PATCH {{host}}/library/20260101-120000-deadbeef
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Sunset over the lake", "collections": ["c-1a2b3c4d"]}

### Delete a collection — the photos stay in the library
DELETE {{host}}/collections/c-1a2b3c4d

### --- Device settings (also editable from Home Assistant) --------------------

### Current settings + their valid values
GET {{host}}/prefs

### The frame now hangs vertically (also re-shows the current photo)
PATCH {{host}}/prefs
Content-Type: application/json

{"orientation": "portrait"}

### Only crop when cover throws away less than 20% of the photo
PATCH {{host}}/prefs
Content-Type: application/json

{"fit": "auto", "auto_fit_max_crop": 0.2}
